 "process_note": "Disclosed: the first held-out run used lower floors (smoke 0.1, glass 0.1, fire 0.1) and showed false smoke alarms from screams and timers. The floors were raised to the plan's values (smoke 0.35, glass 0.3, fire 0.3) and the same simulator is also reported on development clips (scenarios_dev), so the change can be checked on data not used to report.",
 "limits": [
  "No recordings of real falls (body hitting a floor): the crash is breaking glass, and a fall that makes little sound will be missed.",
  "Smoke and CO alarms are synthetic NFPA 72 tones mixed with household noise and simple echo, not recordings of real alarms.",
  "No shouting-for-help clips: the shout detector has no measured catch rate and never raises an alert on its own.",
  "Clips are close-microphone public recordings, joined in software; no real kitchen or real room has been measured yet."
 ]
